From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <stefdo61@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:45:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 103/119] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: add NSS reserved memory

The UBI32 network subsystem loads its firmware at a fixed physical
address of 0x40000000 and uses the region below it for its descriptor
rings.  Reserve 16 MiB there, matching the downstream QSDK layout for
IPQ5018 (single UBI core).

Signed-off-by: Stefan <stefdo61@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
index c95c5ccad..968732029 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -137,6 +137,11 @@ reserved-memory {
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
 
+		nss_region: memory@40000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x1000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		tz_apps@4a400000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x4a400000 0x0 0x400000>;
 			no-map;
